# Environment for forgejo-backup.service and forgejo-backup-verify.service.
#
# Copy to /etc/default/forgejo-backup on the VPS. The unit reads it with
# `EnvironmentFile=-`, so the file is OPTIONAL: with it absent, or with
# every line below commented out, both units behave exactly as they did
# before this file existed — a local-only backup and a local verify.
#
#   scp systemd/forgejo-backup.env.example root@<vps>:/etc/default/forgejo-backup
#   ssh root@<vps> chmod 600 /etc/default/forgejo-backup
#   ssh root@<vps> $EDITOR /etc/default/forgejo-backup
#
# systemd parses this file itself, not a shell: no `export`, no quoting
# tricks, no command substitution. One KEY=value per line.

# --- off-host copy ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# The gap this closes: without it every copy of the backup lives on the disk
# being backed up, which protects against a broken database and not against
# losing the VPS.
#
# rsync destination (default tool). Either a local path on another mount, or
# an ssh target. The trailing slash matters to rsync.
#OFFHOST_DEST=u123456@u123456.your-storagebox.de:forgejo/
#
# rclone destination instead. A `remote:path` with no `@` and no `/` before
# the colon is detected as rclone automatically when rclone is installed;
# set OFFHOST_TOOL to override the guess either way.
#OFFHOST_DEST=storagebox:forgejo/
#OFFHOST_TOOL=rclone
#
# borg instead (the fleet's tool; encrypted at rest, deduplicated, retention
# on the box). Decided 2026-09-15, anki-sync/ROADMAP.md. Needs the library
# at /usr/local/lib/borg-offhost.sh, the VPS's own storage-box key, and the
# passphrase file (root, 0600) that BORG_PASSCOMMAND reads.
#OFFHOST_DEST=ssh://storagebox/./backup/vps
#OFFHOST_TOOL=borg
#BORG_PASSCOMMAND=cat /etc/borg/passphrase
#BORG_RSH=ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_storagebox -o BatchMode=yes
#OFFHOST_PRUNE=--keep-daily 14 --keep-weekly 8 --keep-monthly 12

# How the transfer is confirmed.
#   readback (default) — pull the remote copy back and compare sha256. Works
#                        against storage that offers no shell, and proves the
#                        bytes that arrived are the bytes that left. Costs a
#                        second transfer of the archive each night.
#   none               — copy and hope. The log says so on every run.
#OFFHOST_VERIFY=readback

# ssh needs a key it can use non-interactively as root. Point at it here if
# it is not root's default identity.
#RSYNC_RSH=ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_storagebox -o BatchMode=yes

# --- local behaviour -------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults shown; uncomment only to change them. Once the off-host copy is
# verified, KEEP=3 is enough locally (the 1.1 GB tarballs were most of the
# disk's use at 14).
#SRC=/root/forgejo-server
#DEST=/root/forgejo-backups
#KEEP=14
#CONTAINER=forgejo
